  "subtitle": "A robot chess computer whose invisible under-board X-Y plotter lifts magnetic pieces and moves them 'by magic'",
  "why_scout_cares": "The museum's only 'ghost-mover' chess computer: it senses your moves on a pressure-sensitive board AND physically moves its own pieces with an invisible under-board plotter — pieces slide 'by magic,' with no visible arm. Genuinely distinct from the Fidelity sensory board (senses only) and the Novag Robot Adversary (visible surface gripper arm).",
